                <pb facs="0245" n="179" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg179"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3731/1024</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Western
                        European Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Moffat</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-08-24">August 24, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>With reference to the Swiss Chargé d’Affaires’s call of August 22, I ascertained
                    that the position of this Government would be that our treaty relations with
                    Cuba were on a special footing specifically recognized in all our unconditional
                    most favored nation treaties. Accordingly, no third country would benefit by
                    reductions granted to Cuba.</p>
                <p>I also ascertained that the Department of Agriculture had not yet completed its
                    regulations governing the admission of foodstuffs from abroad as a result of the
                    drought and attendant speculation.</p>
                <p>I informed Mr. Micheli on both these questions Thursday, August 23.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pierrepont Moffat</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
